# NestJS API (`apps/api`)

Package: `@pcms/api`. Entry: `src/main.ts`. Root module: `src/app.module.ts`.

## Architecture

**Hexagonal (ports & adapters)** per feature module. Dependency rule: `domain` ← `application` ← `infrastructure` / Nest composition root. Never the reverse.

```text
src/modules/<feature>/
├── domain/                 # plain models (no Nest/TypeORM)
├── application/
│   ├── ports/              # interfaces + injection tokens (*.port.ts)
│   └── *.service.ts        # use cases; depend on ports only
├── infrastructure/
│   ├── persistence/        # TypeORM adapters + mappers
│   ├── http/               # controllers + DTOs
│   └── …                   # messaging, storage, security, etc.
└── <feature>.module.ts     # wires ports → adapters
```

Shared kernel: `src/domain/` (enums, `User`). Cross-cutting Nest concerns stay in `src/common/`. TypeORM entities remain in `src/database/entities/` (persistence detail).

## Conventions

- Global prefix: `/api` (set in `main.ts`)
- Config via `ConfigService`: `config.get('database.host')` — namespaces in `src/config/configuration.ts`
- Validation: `class-validator` DTOs in `infrastructure/http/dto/` + global `ValidationPipe`
- Auth: JWT access token in body; refresh in HttpOnly SameSite=Strict cookie
- RBAC: `@Roles()` + `RolesGuard`; public routes via `@Public()`
- Rate limiting: `@nestjs/throttler` on sensitive auth routes
- Content: Markdown via `HtmlRendererPort` (marked adapter); sanitize with DOMPurify (`content.util.ts`)
- Media: `ImageProcessorPort` + `FileStoragePort` (Sharp / local disk under `MEDIA_LOCAL_PATH`)
- Application layer may use Nest `@Injectable` and HTTP exceptions; must not import TypeORM, BullMQ, bcrypt, sharp, fs, or marked directly

## Database

- Entities: `src/database/entities/`
- Migrations: `src/database/migrations/` — use TypeORM CLI scripts in `package.json`
- Do **not** rely on `synchronize: true` in production paths; use migrations

## Observability

- Logging: Pino via `nestjs-pino`
- Metrics: Prometheus at `/metrics` (not under `/api`)
- Tracing: OpenTelemetry — loaded via `tracing.ts` before `main.ts`
- Health: `@nestjs/terminus` — liveness vs readiness; Redis via `CACHE_HEALTH` port

## Adding endpoints

```typescript
// ✅ Thin HTTP adapter → application service
@Controller('posts')
export class PostsController {
  constructor(private readonly postsService: PostsService) {}

  @Get('admin')
  @Roles(UserRole.ADMIN, UserRole.EDITOR)
  findAllAdmin() {
    return this.postsService.findAllAdmin();
  }
}
```

- Permission-check every new route
- Return data through existing interceptors/filters
- Bind new ports in the feature `*.module.ts`
- Add `*.spec.ts` beside each testable unit — mock **ports** in application specs; mock TypeORM/etc. in adapter specs — **100% coverage** on included paths

## Testing (Jest)

- Colocate: `foo.service.spec.ts` next to `foo.service.ts`
- Setup: `jest.setup.ts` (reflect-metadata, DOMPurify mock)
- Excluded from coverage: `main.ts`, `*.module.ts`, DTOs, entities, enums, ports, models, `src/domain/**`, migrations
- Run: `npm run test:cov -w @pcms/api`

## Anti-patterns

- Application/domain importing TypeORM, BullMQ, or framework-specific I/O libraries
- New global providers without wiring in `AppModule`
- Raw SQL when TypeORM repository adapter suffices
- Skipping validation DTOs on POST/PATCH bodies
- Returning unsanitized HTML from user Markdown
- Integration tests in `test/` folder (empty — use unit mocks unless harness is added)
